## Evidence boundary

The record does not reveal a completed price for an affordable two-DIA firm, job-level margins, the distribution of DIA certificates among companies, or whether a particular seller and key employees will stay. The recent Advies Lieren/Buro Pear announcement shows a continuity structure, while the register independently confirms both certified entities. It does not disclose consideration, payroll, customer retention or post-close economics. The partner payment and target documents in the ninety-day test must settle those points.

The Bbl duty is standing. The August 2026 amendment is enacted and current, but its official explanation says it only updates a standard reference and adds no administrative burden. Neither the rule, certificate counts nor public credit ceilings establish customer budget or lender approval.

