 succeeded in 94ms:
   100	<p>Audit load also steps up with delivery. The current table requires four annual project-site assessments for a branch with one or two DIAs and fewer than 500 reports. It rises to six for three to five DIAs or 500–1,100 reports. <!-- CHECK: 06-audit-load --> Growth buys more announced and unannounced scrutiny, not merely utilisation.</p>
   101	<p>The founder bottleneck is retaining qualified judgement while refusing to interfere with it. Hiring, route design, debtor control and portfolio sales can be delegated. The technical signature cannot be automated into an owner permission. If customer twenty still calls the seller personally, the acquisition has not transferred.</p>
   102	</section>
   103	
   104	<section class="competition">
   105	<h2>The incumbent gets a turn</h2>
   106	<p>The strongest competitor is another certified acquirer. Advies Lieren's purchase of Buro Pear shows the response: combine specialist knowledge and customers, keep project leadership during transition, then move work onto an existing qualified bench. <!-- CHECK: 06-precedent-sale --> Such a buyer can pay for synergies that the reader does not have.</p>
   107	<p>Broader firms compete differently. Tritium markets asbestos work inside a team spanning soil, environment and sustainability, and its DIA vacancy describes projects from buildings to whole housing districts. <!-- CHECK: 06-dia-salary --> A property manager may prefer one supplier across hazardous materials and environmental work. A demolition contractor can repeatedly introduce its established independent inventory bureau without owning it.</p>
   108	<p>The small incumbent can respond too. Asdesk publishes fixed prices and promises an experienced certified inspector, accredited laboratory work and a clear report. <!-- CHECK: 06-retail-price --> HMP advertises structural access to freelancers. <!-- CHECK: 06-hmp-demand --> One has transparent retail acquisition; the other has variable capacity. The buyer must find a target with a transferable customer book, not assume that better scheduling is novel.</p>
   109	<p>Partner capture begins before purchase. An overflow partner learns which leads convert and can decline the introduction fee. After acquisition, demolition firms and property managers can demand lower prices because they control job flow. Laboratories can lengthen turnaround or raise sample charges. None of these parties needs to buy the company for its margin to shrink.</p>
   110	</section>
   111	
   112	<div class="counter">
   113	<div class="case-head"><span class="who">The capable failure</span></div>
   114	<p>The buyer finds a respected two-DIA bureau. Both inspectors sign retention agreements. Customers accept the change, reports remain sound and audits pass. The reader improves scheduling and wins several portfolio accounts. Execution is competent.</p>
   115	<p>A certified strategic buyer could still have paid more. It already has technical cover, Dutch management, a quality function and spare route capacity. It can spread those costs across more reports and move work when one DIA is ill. The reader must fund the same resilience inside a small standalone company.</p>
   116	<p>To win the auction, the reader accepts the seller's EBITDA before replacing the seller's work and borrows against it. Twelve months later the seller leaves as agreed. A retained DIA becomes technical final responsible, receives the deserved raise and reduces field days for review. Revenue holds, yet replacement labour and debt service consume the cash. Nothing failed in sales, safety or diligence. The wrong owner had a structurally higher cost base than the strategic bidder.</p>
   117	</div>
   118	
   119	<section class="monday">
   120	<h2>The first ninety days</h2>
   121	<ol>
   122	<li><strong>Days 1–15:</strong> call three certification bodies, five owners from the public register and two acquisition advisers. Confirm in writing how a share transfer, director change, technical-final-responsible change and employee departure are handled. Spend at most a <strong>€500 advice-and-travel hurdle</strong>.</li>
   123	<li><strong>Days 10–30:</strong> recruit one certified partner. Agree a transparent €100 completed-introduction hurdle, customer ownership, data handling and the rule that the partner scopes, contracts, inspects and signs. The reader never appears certified.</li>
   124	<li><strong>Days 20–50:</strong> approach the ten prospect types. Qualify five real pre-1994 projects with planned works. Broker one inspection at the partner's quoted price and obtain the introduction fee only after the customer pays.</li>
   125	<li><strong>Days 30–65:</strong> screen fifteen certified firms from the register. Seek two with at least two employed DIAs, a separate Dutch customer owner and repeat B2B revenue. Reject seller-only practices before asking price.</li>
   126	<li><strong>Days 50–80:</strong> offer a <strong>€2,500 diligence-budget hurdle</strong> for an accountant and employment or certification specialist to review one anonymised target pack. Rebuild three years of EBITDA after €75,000 per missing senior-DIA role and €85,000 founder replacement.</li>
   127	<li><strong>Days 75–90:</strong> ask the best owner and each critical employee separately about twelve-month plans, pay, authority and change of control. Draft a non-binding structure capped at €50,000 reader equity, with retention and customer continuity as closing conditions. Total pre-evidence spend stays below <strong>€4,500</strong>. Do not resign or sign a purchase agreement.</li>
   128	</ol>
   129	<p><strong>Pass:</strong> one real customer pays the certified partner, the partner pays the introduction fee, and one target supplies payroll, certificate, job-level margin and customer-retention evidence. It has two independently staying DIAs, one qualifying as technical final responsible, and shows at least €150,000 EBITDA before any missing seller-DIA normalisation. The €300,000 structure must still pay founder replacement and debt service. <strong>Kill:</strong> no paid inspection after five qualified projects; no target has two staying DIAs; the only technical signatory is the departing seller; normalised cash misses debt service; or all credible targets require more than €50,000 reader capital at risk. The experiment runs beside the job. Closing does not.</p>
   130	</section>
   131	
   132	<div class="verdict-box">
   133	<h2>Verdict</h2>
   134	<p class="verdict"><strong>ACQUIRE, DO NOT BUILD</strong></p>
   135	<p>The standing obligation, employed-DIA rule and physical report make this a real operating business, but they do not grant the reader a personal route. Buy only a team and customer book that already work without the seller. The single assumption that would most change the verdict is that an affordable target exists with two independently staying DIAs and at least €150,000 of pre-normalisation EBITDA. If the search finds only owner-DIA practices or strategic-buyer prices, do not enter.</p>
   136	</div>
   137	
   138	<div class="reading">
   139	<h2>Reading</h2>
   140	<ul>
   141	<li>Informatiepunt Leefomgeving, <a href="https://iplo.nl/regelgeving/regels-voor-activiteiten/sloopactiviteit/asbestinventarisatieplicht/">asbestos-inventory duty under the Bbl</a> and <a href="https://iplo.nl/thema/asbest/lavs/over-het-lavs/stappen-lavs/">LAVS process</a>.</li>
   142	<li>Staatscourant, <a href="https://zoek.officielebekendmakingen.nl/stcrt-2026-29952.html">2026 process-certificate scheme for asbestos inventory and removal</a>.</li>
   143	<li>Ascert, <a href="https://www.ascert.nl/certificaatregister">live certificate totals</a> and <a href="https://www.ascert.nl/zoek-een-certificaat?certificatenumber=&amp;city=&amp;company=asbest&amp;postalcode=&amp;type=processcertificate">company register</a>.</li>
   144	<li>ProXia, <a href="https://www.proxia.nl/examens/asbest-examens/dia-examen/">DIA examination requirements</a>.</li>
   145	<li>HMP Asbestinventarisatie, <a href="https://www.hmp-asbest.nl/vacatures/">freelance DIA recruitment</a>; Asdesk, <a href="https://www.asdesk.nl/Prijslijst%202026.pdf">2026 price list</a>.</li>
   146	<li>CREON Groep / Tritium Advies, <a href="https://vacatures.creongroep.nl/o/deskundig-inventariseerder-asbest-dia">DIA vacancy and salary range</a>.</li>
   147	<li>Advies Lieren, <a href="https://www.asbest-lieren.nl/overname-buro-pear/">acquisition of Buro Pear</a>.</li>
   148	<li>Brookz, <a href="https://www.brookz.nl/branche-informatie/asbestbedrijf">asbestos-business sale page and indicative multiples</a>.</li>
   149	<li>Qredits, <a href="https://www.qredits.nl/zakelijk-krediet/mkb-krediet">MKB credit terms</a>.</li>
   150	<li>KVK, <a href="https://www.kvk.nl/verkopen-en-overnemen/zo-kijkt-een-koper-naar-je-cijfers-tijdens-het-boekenonderzoek/">buyer due diligence and owner dependence</a>.</li>
   151	</ul>
   152	</div>
   153	
